          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.6,
            0.846,
            0.657
          ],
          "content": "In the second case, the distance d between the ant and the laddu can be calculated using the Baudhayana Theorem, since we have a right triangle here."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.472,
            0.653,
            0.601,
            0.674
          ],
          "content": "d ^ { 2 } = 2 4 ^ { 2 } + 3 2 ^ { 2 }",
          "image_source": "images/page_17_equation_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.477,
            0.679,
            0.654,
            0.699
          ],
          "content": "d = \\sqrt{1600} = 40   cm",
          "image_source": "images/page_17_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.706,
            0.847,
            0.764
          ],
          "content": "We see that in each of these unfoldings, the lengths of the line segments between the ant and the laddu are different! So we have to carefully list all the possible different unfoldings to find the answer!"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
